# NIGHTGATE: Environment variables

# ── Network & node ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# preview | testnet | preprod | mainnet | undeployed. Preprod and mainnet need the
# node and indexer below (your own, or hosted ones with the access token in the URL,
# see docs/self-hosted.md); preview has public ones built in. Startup names
# what is missing, so leave a line commented rather than filling in a placeholder.
NIGHTGATE_NETWORK=preprod
# NIGHTGATE_NODE_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:9944
# hosted node, with the access token in the query:
# NIGHTGATE_NODE_URL=wss://<node-host>?token=<token>

# ── Midnight Indexer (GraphQL) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The HTTP URL alone is enough: the ws subscription endpoint is derived from it
# (ws scheme, /ws after the path, the query kept). Set NIGHTGATE_INDEXER_WS_URL
# only if your indexer serves subscriptions somewhere non-standard.
# NIGHTGATE_INDEXER_HTTP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8088/api/v4/graphql
# hosted indexer, with the access token in the query:
# NIGHTGATE_INDEXER_HTTP_URL=https://<indexer-host>/api/v4/graphql?token=<token>

# Disable the block crawler (true by default)
NIGHTGATE_CRAWLER_ENABLED=false

# ── Submission stack ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Proving is fully in-process (wasm) by default: no proof server needed,
# proving keys download from Midnight's S3 on first use, tens of seconds to
# minutes of CPU per proof. For production run the proof-server container (compose:
# midnightntwrk/proof-server on :6300); configuring its URL selects server
# proving automatically. NIGHTGATE_PROVING_MODE=server|wasm overrides.
# NIGHTGATE_PROOF_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:6300
# NIGHTGATE_PROVING_MODE=wasm
# HTTP timeout of ONE proof request in server mode (ms, default 300000 = 5 min;
# the SDK re-requests a timed-out proof up to 3x). Raise together with the
# proof-server container's job TTL (seconds, default 600) for slow circuits.
# NIGHTGATE_PROOF_TIMEOUT_MS=300000
# MIDNIGHT_PROOF_SERVER_JOB_TIMEOUT=600
# NIGHTGATE_ZK_CONFIG_BASE=./contracts
# NIGHTGATE_PRIVATE_STATE_BACKEND=cap-db               # cap-db (default) | level
# Max time the connectWalletForSigning prewarm job waits for the wallet to sync
# to the chain tip before failing. Raise for far-behind / cold-sync wallets.
# NIGHTGATE_PREWARM_SYNC_TIMEOUT_MS=43200000           # default 12h
# Bounded sync gate for facade-backed READ actions (getWalletBalance + fee
# estimates): a still-syncing wallet answers 503 WALLET_SYNCING after this
# wait instead of blocking the request. 0 or negative disables the gate.
# NIGHTGATE_WALLET_READ_SYNC_TIMEOUT_MS=10000           # default 10s

# ── Crypto ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 32-byte hex secret used to encrypt viewing/seed keys at rest (AES-256-GCM).
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Keep it STABLE once set: a changed key (or the per-process dev fallback when
# unset) can't decrypt the persisted wallet sync-state, forcing a cold resync.
# In production srv/utils/crypto.ts throws if this is unset.
ENCRYPTION_KEY=REPLACE_WITH_OUTPUT_OF_openssl_rand_hex_32


# ── Scripts: wallet sync / deploy-e2e / probe-indexer ─────────────────────
# Consumed by scripts/start-wallet-sync.mjs, scripts/run-deploy-e2e.mjs,
# scripts/derive-keys.mjs, scripts/probe-indexer.mjs. .env should be
# gitignored — NEVER commit a real wallet seed or mnemonic.
NIGHTGATE_URL=http://localhost:4004
LACE_VIEWING_KEY=XXXXX
LACE_SEED_HEX=XXXXX
# LACE_MNEMONIC=
# INDEXER_URL=
# The node the compose `indexer` service reads (same network): your own, or a hosted one with its token
# INDEXER_UPSTREAM_NODE_URL=ws://<node-host>:9944
NIGHTGATE_REPLICA_COUNT=1
# Emergency migration window only. Production SQLite otherwise fails closed.
# NIGHTGATE_ALLOW_PRODUCTION_SQLITE=false
# Optional stable label shown by health/readiness/log correlation.
# NIGHTGATE_INSTANCE_ID=nightgate-primary
